# Sentinel Security - Git Exclusion Rules
#
# This file specifies which files and directories Git should
# ignore when tracking changes and uploading code to GitHub.
# It prevents temporary files, virtual environments, and
# sensitive configuration files from being committed.
#
# These rules help keep the repository clean and reduce
# the risk of accidentally exposing private information.